ITEMS=[]
def family(options,rows):
 assert len(options)==len(rows)==4
 for i,(q,e) in enumerate(rows):ITEMS.append((q,[options[i]]+options[:i]+options[i+1:],e))
family(['Prescribed safe storage','Complete covering in public','Effective personal control','Safe custody of the keys'],[
('An ordinary licensed firearm will be left at home while its owner is away and is not under anyone\'s lawful direct personal control. Which requirement directly governs where it must be kept?','Regulation86 requires prescribed safe or strongroom storage when the firearm is not under direct personal and physical control, unless a specific exception applies.'),
('A lawfully carried handgun is in an appropriate holder and remains controlled, but part of the firearm is visible in a public place. Which section84requirement is not satisfied?','Section84 requires the firearm to be completely covered as well as carried in an appropriate holder under effective control.'),
('A firearm is covered in an appropriate carrier in public, but the carrier is left where the licence holder cannot exercise control over it. Which carrying requirement is missing?','Covering and a suitable holder do not replace the separate obligation of effective control.'),
('A firearm is properly locked away, but the owner leaves the safe key accessible to unauthorised visitors. Which separate custody obligation has been neglected?','Section120(8) addresses keeping safe keys in safe custody, as well as locking the firearm away.')])
family(['The authorised storage period','The reason for the storage','The parties\' identifying details','The firearm and licence particulars'],[
('A proposed regulation86(4)storage authorisation identifies the people, firearm and reason but gives no start or end period. What required information is missing?','The written authorisation must specify the period for which storage is allowed.'),
('A storage authorisation gives dates and identifies the parties and firearm but never explains why the temporary arrangement is needed. What required information is missing?','Regulation86(4)(c) requires the reason for storage as well as its period and identifying details.'),
('A storage document identifies the firearm and dates but omits the storage provider\'s identity number and physical address. Which required information is incomplete?','The authorisation must identify both relevant persons by name, identity number and physical address.'),
('A storage document names both people and provides a reason and period, but only says "one firearm" without sufficient identifying information. What required particulars are missing?','The document must sufficiently identify the firearm and the licence, permit or authorisation concerned.')])
family(['Written authority from the lawful holder','Endorsement by the relevant DFO','A prescribed safe at the named place','The storage provider\'s qualifying status'],[
('A licence holder wants another licensed person to store a firearm under regulation86(4), but the proposed document was written only by a neighbour without authority from the holder. Which requirement is missing?','The written authorisation must come from the person legally entitled to possess the firearm.'),
('Both parties have signed an otherwise complete regulation86(4)storage arrangement, but no firearms officer has endorsed it. What approval is still needed?','The holder\'s written authorisation must be endorsed by the relevant Designated Firearms Officer.'),
('An endorsed storage authorisation names one address, but the provider proposes storing the firearm at a different unapproved address. Which requirement would be breached?','The firearm must be in a prescribed safe at the place specified in the authorisation.'),
('A person with no firearm licence or relevant muzzle-loading competency offers storage under regulation86(4). Written consent alone is proposed. Which threshold requirement is absent?','The storage provider must have the qualifying status specified in regulation86(4), in addition to the written endorsed authority and proper safe.')])
family(['Storage does not permit use','Removal is limited to authorised persons','Transport must follow the authorisation','The DFO may cancel on good cause'],[
('A person authorised only to store another owner\'s firearm asks to take it for personal practice during the storage period. Which regulation86(4)restriction answers that request?','A firearm stored under that provision may not be used by the storage provider or anyone else while so stored.'),
('An uninvolved friend offers to take a firearm out of a regulation86(4)safe, although the friend is neither its lawful holder nor a person granted the relevant permission. Which restriction applies?','Removal is limited to the lawful holder or the person granted the specified permission; another friend is not automatically authorised.'),
('The endorsed storage arrangement permits a qualifying person to move a firearm to and from the named safe on specified conditions. What controls that movement?','The2012amendment permits the relevant authorised person to transport only as authorised by the Registrar or DFO.'),
('A relevant DFO identifies good cause why a temporary-storage arrangement should no longer continue. What power does regulation86(4)(d)provide?','The relevant DFO may cancel the storage permission at any time on good cause.')])
family(['A compliant safe or strongroom','A DFO certificate for a qualifying existing safe','A prescribed joint-access lock-away safe','Direct personal and physical control'],[
('For ordinary home storage when a licensed firearm is not personally controlled, what is the standard storage facility required by regulation86(1)?','The default is a safe or strongroom conforming to the referenced SABS standards, subject to specific regulatory provisions.'),
('An owner relies on an existing safe approved under the previous law. What formal recognition is required for the relevant deemed-compliance provision, rather than assuming its age is enough?','Under regulation86(8), as amended, the DFO must issue the relevant certificate for a qualifying existing safe.'),
('At premises with a lawful firearm-control arrangement, the alternative locker is designed to open only with the cooperation of both the designated person and the holder. Which prescribed alternative is described?','Regulation86(5) allows a prescribed installed lock-away safe requiring joint opening, alongside the compliant safe or strongroom option.'),
('An owner asserts that the default storage rule has not been triggered because the firearm remains under the owner\'s immediate bodily supervision. Which factual condition is relevant to that claim?','The regulation distinguishes prescribed storage from direct personal and physical control. Mere ownership or being somewhere in the house is not the same condition.')])
family(['The firearm must be secured','The ammunition must be secured','The licence must remain legible','The access key must remain controlled'],[
('An owner puts all ammunition in the compliant safe but leaves the firearm unattended in an ordinary drawer, with no exception applying. Which item still needs the prescribed custody?','Securing ammunition alone does not satisfy the storage duty for the unattended firearm.'),
('A firearm is correctly locked away, but its ammunition is left unsecured outside the prescribed storage, with no exception applying. Which separate item remains improperly stored?','Regulation86(1) applies to the firearm and its ammunition.'),
('An owner\'s firearms and ammunition are secure, but the licence is allowed to become unreadable through damage. Which document-related duty remains unsatisfied?','Section106 requires the licence, permit or authorisation to be maintained in an undefaced and legible condition.'),
('A compliant safe contains the firearm and ammunition, but its key is handed to an unauthorised person. Which access-control element must be corrected?','Safe storage includes safe custody of the key; the physical safe alone is insufficient if access is uncontrolled.')])
family(['An appropriate handgun holder','An appropriate holder for the other firearm','Complete covering of the firearm','Effective control by the carrier'],[
('A person lawfully carries a handgun in public. Which requirement addresses the kind of holster, rucksack or similar carrier used, rather than visibility or control?','Section84(1)(a) specifies the permitted type of handgun holder, including an appropriate attached holster or a rucksack or similar holder.'),
('A person lawfully carries a firearm other than a handgun in public. Which carrier requirement is specified by section84(1)(b)?','It must be in a holder designed, manufactured or adapted for carrying that firearm, as well as covered and controlled.'),
('An owner argues that an appropriate holster alone makes a visibly exposed firearm compliant with section84. What additional requirement directly addresses visibility?','The firearm must be completely covered. An appropriate holder does not eliminate that requirement.'),
('A suitable covered firearm carrier is within view but beyond the person\'s ability to supervise or control effectively. Which section84requirement still needs attention?','The person carrying the firearm must be able to exercise effective control; visibility from a distance is not enough by itself.')])
family(['Unloaded storage is required in this case','The section13exception is relevant','The collector exception is relevant','The facts are insufficient to assume an exception'],[
('An ordinary section15licence holder, who is not a collector and has no other relevant exception, stores the firearm at home. What does regulation86(11)(a)require concerning its loaded state?','Firearms outside the stated exceptions must be stored unloaded. This scenario expressly excludes the exceptions.'),
('A lawful owner asks whether regulation86(11)(a)imposes the same unloaded-storage requirement on a firearm licensed specifically for self-defence under section13. Which provision matters?','The unloaded-storage provision expressly distinguishes section13firearms. This does not remove the other safe-custody obligations.'),
('A qualifying collector considers keeping one loaded firearm in the safe for self-defence. Which addition in the2012amendment is relevant to this legal question?','The amended regulation includes a collector exception for one loaded firearm in the safe for self-defence; other custody requirements remain.'),
('An owner says only that a firearm is "for protection" but gives no licence category or collector status. Can an unloaded-storage exception be concluded from those words alone?','The legal category and conditions matter; a casual description of purpose does not establish a statutory exception.')])
family(['A licence for a compatible firearm','A permit to possess ammunition','A relevant licensed trade authority','Another lawful authorisation'],[
('An ordinary owner relies on section90(a)to possess ammunition. What relationship must exist between the ammunition and the firearm covered by the owner\'s licence?','The licensed firearm must be capable of discharging that ammunition; a licence for an unrelated firearm is not sufficient under that paragraph.'),
('A person relies on a specific ammunition-possession permit rather than a licence for an ordinary personal firearm. Which section90basis is being used?','Section90(b) recognises a permit to possess ammunition as a distinct lawful basis.'),
('A properly licensed dealer possesses ammunition as part of the lawful dealership. Which section90basis is relevant, apart from an individual personal firearm licence?','Section90(c) includes relevant dealer and other listed trade or transport authorities.'),
('A person has a valid authority under the Act that lawfully permits the ammunition possession but is not relying on the personal-licence or permit categories in the question. Which residual section90basis applies?','Section90(d) recognises a person who is otherwise lawfully authorised. A mere personal belief or shop receipt is not such authority.')])
family(['The ordinary200-cartridge ceiling','The dedicated-status exception','Specific permission from the Registrar','Ammunition bought and used at an accredited range'],[
('A licensed ordinary owner has no dedicated or professional status, no quantity authorisation and no applicable range exception. What rule governs the maximum cartridge quantity for each licensed firearm?','Section91(1) sets the ordinary ceiling at200cartridges for each licensed firearm, subject to the express exceptions.'),
('A licensed dedicated sports person considers the section91quantity limit. Which status-based provision is relevant?','Section91(2)(a) exempts qualifying dedicated hunters, dedicated sports persons and professional hunters holding a licence from the ordinary ceiling.'),
('An ordinary licence holder without dedicated status shows good cause for possessing more than200cartridges for a licensed firearm. Which statutory route addresses that request?','The Registrar may authorise a larger quantity on good cause; the person must obtain that authority rather than merely decide to exceed the limit.'),
('A licence holder buys ammunition at an accredited shooting range and discharges that ammunition there. Which express exception addresses that ammunition?','Section91(2)(b) concerns ammunition bought and discharged at an accredited range, not an unlimited quantity taken home.')])
family(['The quantity limit is satisfied','The quantity limit would be exceeded','The compatibility requirement is missing','The range exception does not cover taking it home'],[
('An ordinary owner has exactly200cartridges for a compatible licensed firearm and meets all other requirements. No exception is needed. What is the position under the numerical ceiling alone?','The prohibition is on more than200cartridges; exactly200does not exceed that ceiling.'),
('An ordinary owner has190cartridges for a licensed firearm and proposes adding a sealed box of25, with no exemption or authorisation. What is the result under the quantity limit?','190+25=215, exceeding the ordinary200-cartridge ceiling. Packaging does not change the count.'),
('An owner has only20cartridges, but none can be discharged by any firearm covered by the owner\'s licences, and no other authority exists. What is the legal issue despite the small quantity?','The quantity ceiling does not itself authorise possession. Section90requires an appropriate possession basis, including compatibility under paragraph(a).'),
('An ordinary owner already holds the maximum permitted quantity and buys additional ammunition at an accredited range, intending to take it all home unused. Why is the range exception insufficient on these facts?','The exception covers ammunition bought and discharged at the accredited range. Buying there alone does not exempt unused take-home ammunition.')])
family(['Failure to secure the firearm itself','Failure to protect safe keys','Failure to prevent loss while controlled','Noncompliance with the authorised storage address'],[
('An unattended firearm is stolen from an unlocked ordinary cabinet because the owner never placed it in prescribed storage. Which custody failure most directly explains the breach?','Section120(8) addresses failure to lock away a firearm when it is not carried or directly controlled.'),
('A firearm is stolen after an owner leaves the safe key in an openly accessible location. The safe itself meets the prescribed standard. Which custody failure is directly identified?','The Act expressly addresses failure to keep the keys in safe custody; a compliant safe does not excuse insecure key handling.'),
('While carrying a firearm, an owner takes no reasonable precautions against loss and is dispossessed through that failure. Which separate section120(8)obligation is implicated?','Reasonable precautions against loss or theft apply while the firearm is carried or under direct control, not only while it is stored.'),
('A storage provider has an endorsed permission for one address but moves the firearm to a different safe without authority. Which aspect of the storage permission has been breached?','The permission is tied to the named place. Another safe does not automatically satisfy the location condition.')])
assert len(ITEMS)==48
